# VPS-only runtime state that happens to live inside this same directory
# (the Docker build context is the whole repo root, "context: ." in
# docker-compose.prod.yml) — never meant to be sent to the build. Skipping
# .docker-data especially matters: without it, every build tries to tar up
# Docker's own data-root (see DEPLOY.md), which contains sockets/pipes tar
# can't archive and enough data to exhaust disk space building the context.
.docker-data
.local-storage
backups
